ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1031 "Triple Integrals Over Type II Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1033 2141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050524 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "505d75ff-8395-5a7e-8e48-f2062c75044a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050534 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050534 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050534 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050534 #edb/ref 1031 "The Divergence Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050534 #edb/ref 1033 2135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050534 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "51703412-3999-597b-8a50-c1bd75195c76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8189" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7dcea6be-fd16-5312-b50c-157bafcc2d65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yz\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}{(\\sqrt{2y})}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/04/043adf0ef683c24fbf4680145411d86fa94b52016bee44ac8f08ca7c5ca9f1b7.png)\n\n \n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0ad2f24-6f0c-5d66-9312-5e41840b4fe5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/75/75a76a2dbc34c889335e66623e12b686eb9a255ee0d67f9be0e3792f2650360c.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e19ffe6a0555851c2b05526272beb21dbcdc082a23a2e11809c661666efdf133.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(4-x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((4-x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6-2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[6x-{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(6(1)-{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129026 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129026 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface ![](images/9c/9c7c9aac6c94031d8430a8e8a2e4d3678a640379cdbc173fc5209ea532f3191b.svg) the plane ![](images/6c/6c78648d93eec934cde0f90387e06783c3d777a7a445e39afc2e5fa91bc2ec0c.svg) and the planes ![](images/89/89c97ad93c125fc2b6f61d44fe9a90845fd289329d79d506c857f970d7586540.svg) ![](images/36/36fdd3a0fb618d9692c52fd9bcb6e916441dee88dbce405fb885ec0f7782f047.svg) ![](images/6b/6be447d259b9b63c2cdd7adc4107d7c96ed4df1730890fc1bb5ce7cd585b8ea6.svg) ![](images/e0/e0f55ae8b32c4b9d5e58808c159b7433fd6e5b9db2212ecdf719869ea230a010.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129026 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7883263b-110b-558f-83b2-0f6ec28be2c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129026 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region.\n\nFor each point ![](images/49/494198ee647d85e4442556a23f0c2d56aa601367360c321385ffc94523c47d73.svg) in the rectangular base region\n![](images/2d/2d0c4af57f0ba5e29300533e6ab0d95ce702b9d75bf175cbb9ffdca5f371d634.svg)\nthe variable ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) runs from the surface\n![](images/72/72a6a2c2ba533fff74fe6ff80bafa9db62c3cbbc81f8be01cb7f5846b95f8dc8.svg)\nup to the plane\n![](images/36/3692729086c0564b65a7865e92dc2d5930f72b59abc0ea7634cd6dfa539b71b1.svg)\n\nSo we can write:\n![](images/d7/d7f58e8932311896757dffef5a240cb53a2b5e0b439455dbf83be832c8c15a01.svg)\n\nTherefore, the volume of ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is given by the following triple integral:\n\n![](images/1e/1e0c7ab5158a2e2dab67f2efae6ef29ac6be9e38bb9613c9c00a96d24c377a93.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129205 #